Derek Ray <derek@moot.its.only.a.spamtrap.org> wrote:
> On 2007-12-18, AngleWyrm <anglewyrm@yahoo.com> wrote:
>> Has anyone got a good tutorial on how to get .diff files patched into
>> nethack?
>
> Have a working vanilla 3.4.3 that compiles and runs on your system.
>
> Change to the root of the tree, where you see /src, /dat, /doc/ etc.
>
> Type "patch -p0 </path/to/foobar.diff".
>
> If you get errors, check the top of the patch and add one to the "-p0" 
> parameter for each extraneous directory at the front of the pathnames;
> ie. if the paths look like "nh_orig/src/mcastu.c", then you need to use -p1.

I'd recommend to first use the --dry-run option if available:

 --dry-run  Do not actually change any files; just print what would happen.

In case something doesn't work out it is a PITA to debug with
half-applied patches.

